  "raw_text": "Step 1: The arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is calculated by summing all the numbers and then dividing by the count of numbers.\nStep 2: Given that the arithmetic mean of 7, 2, \\(x\\), and 10 is 9, we can set up the equation for the mean:\n\\[\n\\frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9\n\\]\nStep 3: Multiply both sides of the equation by 4 to eliminate the denominator:\n\\[\n7 + 2 + x + 10 = 36\n\\]\nStep 4: Simplify the left side of the equation:\n\\[\n19 + x = 36\n\\]\nStep 5: Subtract 19 from both sides to solve for \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = 36 - 19\n\\]\nStep 6: Calculate the value of \\(x\\):\n\\[\nx = 17\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{17}<|im_end|>",
